Z||000000||BC-GT||03-26-2001||05:32 PM||||Okay, so my parking brake on my 85 GT is toast, is removal and install straight forward(bolt right in) or is it welded or something crazy. I have a new handle coming in tomorrow, thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||03-26-2001||08:35 PM||||just bolted in far as i can remember||||reg||1
Z||000002||KevinP||03-27-2001||02:14 AM||||had to redo mine last summer; handle, lines and everything, what a pain it was trying to get everything adjusted!  Lines and handle bolt and snap right in, but you will have to play with the equalizer in back to make sure that it fully engages on both wheels.  Best of luck to ya.<P>Kevin<BR>'84 SE bumping 800 watts||||reg||8
Z||000003||BC-GT||03-27-2001||07:58 PM||||Thanks guys, all is well now, works excellent. Will hold the car in gear at least. Here in BC you need the e-brake for your yearly "Aircare" test, if it doesn't work I don't think you can get insurance.<BR>(I pray to the Fiero gods it passes aircare this year) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/album/?id=4292860395&p=4273360442&idx=18"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||kinboyatuwo||03-28-2001||01:46 PM||||A word to the wise<P>do it early<BR>i re did the cables and such in the fall<P>they are seized already<BR>just got worse and worse daily<P>good luck!<P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||4
